<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>The Foundation doesn't acknowledge the complexity because they're not capable of it.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I despise any depiction of the Foundation as a monolithic, incompetent, shallow entity. Do they hold the idiot ball occasionally? Yes, probably more often than they should. But you're telling me that nobody in over 200 years has looked at what they're building and gone &quot;Y'know, maybe we should acknowledge that this is kind of fucked up.&quot;</p>
<p>Stories like this seem to forget that the Foundation is made up of people from hundreds of countries and thousands of backgrounds, and that they're, you know, <em>human beings</em> and not every human being is a deluded psychopath, and not every member of the Foundation is an American who would go along with this. And even if they are, again, &quot;Americans&quot; come from a variety of backgrounds&#8212; I'm half-Polish, I have friends who are part-Scottish or Irish, I have another friend who has German blood in them, and you're telling me that people who aren't of purely &quot;American&quot; descent wouldn't object?</p>
<p>If you want to critique American Exceptionalism, then excellent, it's a horrible philosophy and deserves to have its nose driven into the dirt until it suffocates. But for the love of god, don't portray the Foundation as idiots while you're doing so.</p>
<p>This alone is enough for me to downvote.</p>
