														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3860245">
									

<p>I actually would throw in with Melon on this one, but for dissimilar reasons - I'm positive GWB spoke like this colloquially - to people he was familiar with, to investors, constituents, and coworkers, but I don't feel like he would speak this way *here*.</p>
<p>It's a really unusual scenario - more akin to taking a diplomatic mission to the moon than meeting the press. Heck, I'd venture to say he wouldn't have spoken this way on normal, non-anomalous diplomatic meetings to other countries, or even to meet with governors.</p>
<p>I haven't exactly studied up upon GWB's speaking patterns, so I'm willing to acknowledge that I might be hugely wrong on this. As of right now though, it feels like having him speak to the suspended not-corpse of Emperor Norton attached to a machine that both embodies and enables the current state of the spirit of America, and having him speak to it like he's talking to just anybody, risks it feeling more like a caricature of GWB than GWB himself.</p>

							</div>

								
					
