<p>By most accounts he is colloquial and personal even in official meetings with heads of state. Supposedly people who know him, even political opponents, generally agree that he has a gift for making people feel comfortable in direct interactions. I've read that he remembers people's names and salient personal details even if he had only met them once, and genuinely seems to care about people he interacts with (comparisons to labrador retrievers aren't uncommon). This might even explain some of his political success, given his unimpressive (to be charitable) public presence. One might imagine he tried to communicate with the public in the same way he talks to anybody, but &quot;non-threatening unremarkable understanding dude&quot; is an affect that doesn't scale well.</p>

